d letting you  catch wild pokemon seamlessly either  right off the bat with berries as bait  or through battling is something that i  would love to see taking the open world  a step further though and letting  players explore or discover different  parts of the region at their own  discretion would be a radical step for  pokemon this is extremely unlikely since  a huge part of the core loop in the main  storylines is unlocking hm certain moves  or some kind of a variant like the noble  pokemon or legends arceus with the  purpose of granting you access to the  later areas in the main game we saw the  possibility of unrestricted exploration  with the beginning steps in a pokemon  game like legends arceus it would be  awesome to see gen 9 build from this  first step and run with it  [Music]  alright not to sound toxic but we can  all agree that with sword and shield and  onward the graphics for pokemon have  been  questionable part of me wants to blame  the switch hardware and there's a lot of  frustration with nintendo's awful online  infrastructure compared to something  like xbox live or ps plus however poor  optimization is definitely on game freak  it would be nice to get a pokemon game  that doesn't look like it belongs on a  gamecube i mean i've been able to look  past this with legends arceus because  the novelty of that game was just so  strong but i'm not sure if i could do it  again  with sword and shield and legends arceus  there have been many cutscenes and story  beats and right now it feels a little  odd with having these cutscenes or  dialogue sequences but without any voice  acting personally if we're going to go  the cutscene route it would be nice to  get full on voice actors in gen 9. if  nothing else maybe it's worth going the  hybrid approach like fire emblem or  breath of the wild where not every line  is spoken aloud instead some sounds or  expressions are conveyed to help make  less important scenes feel more alive  while full-on voiceover can 